ecause  the great end of democratic government  is and I keep repeating this because  it's so important is to serve the people  not just Republicans not just Democrats  so not just one side of an argument or  not just career politicians I mean  here's a problem you know people go to  court politics as a career shouldn't be  it should be as a service last thing I  wanted to touch on what are the simplest  reforms that you favor which would  require the least sort of degree of  overhaul and imposition and consensus  that could  most readily be achieved okay that's a  great question actually because if you  try to reform too many things or all at  once you're going to reform nothing you  know you check the kitchen sink in there  you just obscure and confuse the issue  and you don't get anywhere so I think  that there are two key things and the  first of them perhaps the most important  one of them is reform of the electoral  system in all those democracies which  have the first-past-the-post system like  the US and like the UK and reform it in  such a way that that you don't get  Superman or at Arianism okay but where  you do get a genuine spread of  representation of the kinds of  preferences and choices that a very  diverse society will come up with and  then the governments that are formed on  the basis of that have to be governments  of compromise of working together of  seeking bipartisanship as to be try or  her partisanship or or whatever but in  order to satisfy the aim the demand that  they serve the interests of everybody  not just at one part is one thing and I  think the same thing that goes along  with it is we really really do need to  have a look at the media now I think you  are lucky in the United States America  luckier than we are in the UK because  you have some verifying newspapers like  the New York Times and The Washington  Post our great admiration for them  you've got some broadcasters like CNN  who do a good job  you've got examples of the kin